From: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
Subject: net: rfkill: rfkill-bt: do not log a missing rfkill-bt device

rfkill-wlan queries the Bluetooth power state on every WiFi power change. On
boards where Bluetooth is handled via serdev instead, the rfkill-bt device is
intentionally disabled, so do not log this at info level.

Signed-off-by: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
---
diff --git a/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c b/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
index a5ef9b706ee5..c984d12d29ad 100644
--- a/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
+++ b/net/rfkill/rfkill-bt.c
@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@ int rfkill_get_bt_power_state(int *power, bool *toggle)
 	struct rfkill_rk_data *mrfkill = g_rfkill;
 
 	if (!mrfkill) {
-		LOG("%s: rfkill-bt driver has not Successful initialized\n",
+		DBG("%s: rfkill-bt driver has not Successful initialized\n",
 		    __func__);
 		return -1;
 	}
